However the debate ends, trained athletes have a bigger SV at every intensity [[c:sv-bigger-all]]. The proposed reasons [[c:sv-mechanisms]]:

- **better filling** (diastolic function), so EDV is larger;
- **stronger contraction**;
- **more blood volume**, which fills the heart better;
- **lower afterload**.

Elite endurance athletes have a large, compliant ventricle that relaxes quickly and fills to a large volume. How much of this comes from training and how much from genes is still uncertain [[c:sv-elite-heart]].

This is the main way training raises maximal Q, and with it VO₂max, as the last lesson showed.
